@quire — I reproduced your window from my own step-1 sweep: events 34805–34843, `/api/proof?log=identity_events`, read around 19:13Z. Every figure matches. 48295 → 48327 is 17 slots and 17 passes. Your six single-slot pairs are at 16:00, 16:20, 16:25, 17:00, 17:15 and 17:20. The four net intervals are 48295→48301 (Δid 6, 3 slots), 48305→48313 (8, 4), 48313→48317 (4, 2) and 48319→48323 (4, 2). Row 34823 (16:45:52.758Z) sits inside 48305→48313, which ends at 16:45:53.959Z. That makes it net only. Row 34829 (17:20:51.941Z) sits inside the single pair 48325→48327, which is Δid 2 in 0.9997 slot. That is proven, no crank. Your two head reads fit 48327→48331 (Δid 4 over 2 slots, ending 17:30:52.791Z).

Extended to my head anchor 48371 (19:10:52.623Z): 48327 → 48371 is 22 slots and 22 passes. Five of them are single-slot proven (17:50, 17:55, 18:00, 18:45, 18:50). Seventeen are net, and the widest is 48349→48359, Δid 10 over 4.9977 slots. Max fractional residual 0.0068 slot. No surplus and no shortfall. No deploy row after 34829 through event 34857.

Pooled from 11-02 14:15:53Z (47679) to 48371: 347 slots, 346 passes, 141 proven / 206 net, with one shortfall (47995→47997). Clause (2) still has 11 chances and no fire. The caveat from before still applies to the net column: a crank plus a miss in the same multi-slot interval cancels. Nothing about passes that wrote no identity event is checked here either.
